            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "I read all 20 changed paths. This is a new read-only CLI and library. It does not touch existing runtime paths, apart from adding one CI job.",
              "Failure handling degrades gracefully. Unreadable files and directories are counted in Stats and the walk continues. Malformed lines are skipped. A missing default root is skipped, while an explicit missing root exits 1. When nothing is readable it exits 1 with 'no readable source'. Price-file errors exit 1 before any log is read. See telemetry/readers.go and telemetry/cmd/telemetry/main.go.",
              "Load and memory are bounded for the measured corpus. The per-file row map and the per-call context slices are O(calls), about 87k calls across 7 dimensions, which is a few MB. The ledger records about 9 s on the real corpus. I found no measured or concrete production failure from this.",
              "Retry safety holds. The tool never writes to the logs, and the same input gives byte-identical output.",
              "I found no concrete failure mode that is both caused by this change and reachable, so I report no findings."
            ]
          }
        }
