            "lens": "review-readability",
            "findings": [
              {
                "id": "R2-001",
                "lens": "readability",
                "location": "telemetry/readers.go:178-186",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "readLogs mixes Claude and Pi dedupe semantics in one nested loop body, switching on the source string. Claude keeps the last occurrence per file and Pi keeps the first across the whole root, and the only hint is a one-line doc comment on each exported wrapper. The Duplicates counter is incremented in two different branches with different meanings. A change to either dedupe rule risks breaking the other source. Splitting the per-line handling into per-source helpers would make each rule explicit.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "telemetry/readers.go:178-186",
                  "telemetry/readers.go:19-27"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              },
              {
                "id": "R2-002",
                "lens": "readability",
                "location": "telemetry/cmd/telemetry/main.go:108-121",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "human() sets the 'By day' rule (keep the latest N days) by comparing section.name to a string literal. The rank flag is a separate boolean, so the two mechanisms for limiting rows are inconsistent. Renaming the section silently disables day truncation, and the tests would not catch it with the small fixtures. A dedicated field on the section struct would remove the hidden coupling.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "telemetry/cmd/telemetry/main.go:108-121"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              },
              {
                "id": "R2-003",
                "lens": "readability",
                "location": "telemetry/aggregate.go:63-64",
                "severity": "SUGGESTION",
                "claim": "Aggregator.groups is a [6]map indexed by position, and the same ordering is repeated in the keys array in Add and in the outputs slice in Report. The only link between the three is a trailing comment. Reordering one without the others would silently misassign groupings. Named constants for the dimension indexes would remove that risk.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "telemetry/aggregate.go:63-64",
                  "telemetry/aggregate.go:104-106",
                  "telemetry/aggregate.go:174-175"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Read all 20 changed paths in the patch.",
              "No BLOCKER or CRITICAL readability defects were found. The findings above concern structure that makes later edits error-prone.",
              "The ADR and ODD ledger give the change context. The price estimation constant 1e6 is documented by the unit name usd_per_million_tokens."
            ]
          }
