            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 20 manifest paths for reliability. Every behavior is new code in a new module, so there is no baseline regression surface.",
              "The readers tolerate malformed lines, oversized lines, unreadable files and a missing meta file. telemetry/readers_test.go covers each case with observable Stats and Call assertions.",
              "Output is deterministic. The readers sort by timestamp then ID, group keys are sorted, and floating-point costs are summed in a canonical order. telemetry/aggregate_test.go has shuffled-insertion tests for both recorded and estimated costs.",
              "The CLI exit codes (0, 1, 2), the missing-default-root skip, explicit-root errors, and price-table validation are each asserted in telemetry/cmd/telemetry/main_test.go. The golden files and fixture stats are consistent with the fixture data.",
              "Price parsing rejects duplicate keys, unknown fields, trailing data, NaN, Infinity, negatives, and null or missing rates. telemetry/prices_test.go tests each of these.",
              "Recorded costs are never re-estimated, as asserted in telemetry/aggregate_test.go. Without --prices the JSON omits all estimated_ fields, so the no-prices output keeps its previous shape.",
              "The CI job uses staticcheck v0.7.0 against a go 1.21 module. Whether that works depends on the toolchain, which I cannot verify from this candidate, so I raise no finding."
            ]
          }
